Found under k305 (choices worker, 2026-10-31), reproduced in raudssus/ocp:latest. lib/OCP.pm:19 sets `$YAML::XS::Boolean = 'JSON::PP'`, so a YAML `true`/`false` comes back as a JSON::PP::Boolean. With Cpanel::JSON::XS 4.40 loaded (it is, in the image), that object's `eq` is true against ANY string:

    docker run --rm --entrypoint perl raudssus/ocp:latest -MCpanel::JSON::XS -MYAML::XS -e 'local $YAML::XS::Boolean = "JSON::PP"; my $d = YAML::XS::Load("a: true\n"); print "hetzner" eq $d->{a} ? 1 : 0, "false" eq $d->{a} ? 1 : 0, "\n"'
    # prints 11

So every `$value eq 'word'` check on an ocp.yaml or CR value is passed by a boolean. k305 guarded the ones in OCP::Config (`!ref` before known_type, `_is_choice` for security_level). Still open, per the k305 note: `OCP::Provider->known_type`, OCP::Node around line 200, OCP::Cmd::Apply::AMDGPU around lines 183 and 348, and any other `eq` on loaded YAML/JSON.

