2026-10-31 06:58 Root cause (k314 worker): a Cpanel::JSON::XS bug, not an overload-fallback interplay. Cpanel::JSON::XS (4.40 pinned in cpanfile.snapshot; still unchanged in 4.80, the newest on CPAN, 2026-10-14; the code dates from 4.06, 2018) re-overloads eq/ne/"" on JSON::PP::Boolean in a BEGIN block. Its eq handler starts with
    my ($obj, $op) = $_[2] ? ($_[1], $_[0]) : ($_[0], $_[1]);
but overload always passes the boolean as $_[0]; $_[2] only says it stood on the right. So for `'hetzner' eq $true` the plain string lands in $obj, the boolean in $op, and the 'ref $op' branch returns `$obj ? 1 == $op : 0 == $op`: any Perl-true string eq true, '' and '0' eq false. Boolean on the LEFT works as documented (`$true eq 'hetzner'` 0, `$true eq 'true'` 1). So it bites `'word' eq $v` and `grep { $_ eq $v } @list` (24 such greps in lib/, 112 eq/ne with a variable on the right). Verified in raudssus/ocp:latest (perl 5.042003, JSON::PP 4.16, Cpanel 4.40): before Cpanel loads 'hetzner' eq $true is 0, after it 1. Not intended: Cpanel's own POD says 'true is eq to the string true, SV_YES, or 1/1.0', and its t/25_boolean.t only ever puts the boolean on the left. Worth an upstream report for the maintainer (rurban/Cpanel-JSON-XS) — nothing filed, upstream tracker not read (publish gate).

2026-10-31 07:12 Fix chosen: (a) central, in lib/OCP.pm next to $YAML::XS::Boolean. After `use JSON::MaybeXS ()` (which loads Cpanel first; Cpanel overloads only on its first load), OCP re-installs eq/ne on JSON::PP::Boolean as wrappers that call Cpanel's OWN handlers with ($_[0], $_[1], '') — boolean first, swap flag dropped (eq/ne are symmetric). overload->unimport first, as Cpanel does, so -w says no 'redefined'. Result: a boolean compares as Cpanel's POD says (true eq 'true'/1, false eq 'false'/''/0) on BOTH sides; 'hetzner' eq $true is 0. Why not the listed alternatives: builtin booleans (YAML::XS v0.904 does load/dump them on 5.36+ with $YAML::XS::Boolean unset) are no refs, so the k305 ref guards would take nodes: true for 1 and name: true for '1', and CR booleans from Kubernetes::REST/JSON would still be JSON::PP::Boolean; 'boolean' needs boolean.pm (not in the snapshot) and has the same CR gap; normalising after load has both problems and changes what ocp.yaml writes back. The overload fix covers YAML and JSON in every process that loads OCP (bin/ocp first thing; robocop via OCP::Robocop::Controller) and changes no type. Per-site guards would be 24 grep{$_ eq $v} + ~90 right-hand eq sites to keep guarded forever. Consumers checked, identical before/after in the image: JSON::MaybeXS/JSON::PP/Cpanel encode (true/false), YAML::XS::Dump of loaded and of JSON::PP::true/false (ClusterPolicy path), JSON::MaybeXS::is_bool / JSON::PP::is_bool (Config _shown_value, robocop.enabled check), truth, stringify 1/0, ref JSON::PP::Boolean, decode_json booleans; cmp/sort untouched (Cpanel never overloaded cmp). Rexfile: decodes REX_TASK_PARAMS with JSON::MaybeXS but never loads OCP.pm, so the swap remains THERE; only two right-hand eq in share/Rexfile (lines 653, 896, both CIDR strings) and gpu/ntp params arrive 0/1, so nothing reachable today — for the infra lane (ocp-infra-worker) if the Rexfile ever compares a param on the right of eq. AMDGPU.pm 183/348: Node labels from the API are always strings, so not reachable; now right anyway via the central fix — no change needed in Apply files. Config.pm (clean after k305 4793b76): two comments only, saying the ref guards stay and why. Provider.pm/Node.pm: unchanged, not needed.

